  "modeling_notes": [
    "The ordinary Computer Science major in the Bachelor of Science in Computer Foundations is modeled. Cybersecurity, Information Science, minors, teacher preparation, and five-year graduate paths are excluded.",
    "The catalog's named computer-science major and support courses close at 70 credits on a three-credit choice path: 58 fixed/choice credits before the advanced selection, nine advanced-selection credits, and the three-credit capstone.",
    "The Liberal Learning Core is 40 credits minimum. CPSC 150 supplies its three-credit Logical Reasoning requirement and the required MATH 140/148 plus MATH 240 sequence supplies at least six Mathematical Literacy credits, so 31 additional nonmajor Liberal Learning credits are modeled without double-counting those nine credits.",
    "The B.S. science sequence is separate from the seven-credit Investigating the Natural World Area of Inquiry. The major-required PHYS sequence fills the B.S. sequence; the Area of Inquiry remains in the 31-credit nonmajor Core block.",
    "The fixed CPEN 371W supplies one of the two upper-level Writing Intensive courses. A second WI course is a zero-increment gate within the remaining 19-credit elective capacity."
  ],
